; A body's attitude, with its variational equations: the roll phi and the
; pitch theta of a rigid body turning at the constant body rates p, q and r,
; by the kinematic equations of the 3-2-1 Euler angles,
; d/dt phi = p + (q sin(phi) + r cos(phi)) tan(theta) and
; d/dt theta = q cos(phi) - r sin(phi), with one tangent vector stepped
; beside the state by the same program. All three of the math library's
; radian routines are in its step - sin and cos of phi, tan of theta - and
; their rules in the tangent (M2's build; the study's section 7,
; docs/studies/M2-trig.md): cos(a) * da, (-sin(a)) * da and
; fma(r, r, 1) * da, the routine each reads one the step already computes,
; so one call. It is compiled round rdn, every rounded operation toward
; negative infinity: cos's rule negates sin(a) before its product rounds,
; and -(sin(a) * da), negating after, is the same value under rne, rtz and
; rmm, whose roundings are symmetric about zero, and another under rdn and
; rup, so that the reference holds the rule at an attribute where its
; rounding order is a different value. tan has a pole at theta = +-pi/2, the
; gimbal lock, which no representable theta is.
system attitude
format fp256
round  rdn
state  phi, theta
tangent w
param  p = 1/8, q = 1/4, r = 1/2
let    s = q * sin(phi) + r * cos(phi)
d/dt phi = p + s * tan(theta)
d/dt theta = q * cos(phi) - r * sin(phi)
step   rk4, h = 1/64
